WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:14.108
This short guide shows how a trainer signs the Assessment Summary Record digitally on the TMS. This applies to virtual classes only. Physical classes keep the printed record.

00:00:14.408 --> 00:00:26.404
Open the class in Trainer mode and scroll to the Assessment Summary Record, Virtual Class card. It lists every enrolled learner with the status of the learner's signature and your own.

00:00:26.704 --> 00:00:33.372
First, set up your assessor signature. Click Trainer Signature.

00:00:33.672 --> 00:00:43.772
Check your assessor name, NRIC and the date. Only the last three digits and the letter of your NRIC are printed on the record.

00:00:44.072 --> 00:00:54.748
Draw your signature with your mouse, trackpad or finger, then click Save and Use. It is saved once and reused for every class you sign.

00:00:55.048 --> 00:01:02.652
Back on the roster, set the assessment date, then click Sign beside a learner to sign that learner's record.

00:01:02.952 --> 00:01:07.604
Or click Sign All to sign every learner in the class in one go.

00:01:07.904 --> 00:01:25.516
The counters update and each row shows a Signed PDF link. The TMS fills the Assessor block of the course's summary record template with your name, NRIC, signature and date, and files the PDF in the learner's Assessment Records folder in Google Drive.

00:01:25.816 --> 00:01:40.804
Learners sign their own Candidate block from their course page. Once both have signed, the final PDF carries both signatures. Remember, this digital sign-off is for virtual classes only.
